{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"ccb6e913-8db6-4c48-9e23-427ff492c1e1","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The Intervals.icu OAuth integration issues have been resolved. The root causes and applied fixes have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///private/tmp/h-XnikC3/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **Connect Button 401 Unauthorized (`{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`)**\n   - **Cause:** The \"Connect Intervals.icu\" button was an `\u003ca href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\"\u003e` anchor tag. Browser full-page navigation does not include the `Authorization: Bearer` header stored in `localStorage`, causing `require_user()` to reject the request.\n   - **Fix:** Switched `/api/intervals/auth/init` to an authenticated `POST` endpoint returning `{\"authorize_url\": ...}` as JSON. Updated [static/app.js](file:///private/tmp/h-XnikC3/static/app.js) to call this endpoint via its authenticated `api()` fetch wrapper and navigate via `window.location.assign(...)`.\n\n2. **Authorize URL 400 Invalid Request (`{\"error\": \"invalid_request\"}`)**\n   - **Cause:** Intervals.icu disallows requesting both `:READ` and `:WRITE` for the same scope category (e.g. `ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE` and `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`), as `:WRITE` implies read permissions.\n   - **Fix:** Updated `SCOPES` in [config.py](file:///private/tmp/h-XnikC3/config.py) to `\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"`.\n\n3. **Premature Expiry After 1 Hour (\"expired, reconnect\")**\n   - **Cause:** Intervals.icu tokens do not expire and do not issue refresh tokens. The backend assumed a 3600-second fallback TTL (`DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL`), and the background token refresher expired the connection when it saw `expires_at` elapsed without a refresh token.\n   - **Fix:** In [server.py](file:///private/tmp/h-XnikC3/server.py), tokens without `expires_in` are treated as non-expiring (ignored by the background refresh loop). Lazy invalidation was implemented on `intervals_get()` so that token revocations returning HTTP 401 cleanly transition the athlete's status to `\"expired, reconnect\"`. Standardized the token exchange in `exchange_code()` to supply the required parameters (`client_id`, `client_secret`, and `code`).\n","duration_seconds":209.281561,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":266264,"output_tokens":6736,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":1611457,"total_tokens":273000}}}
